0 Two-Speed Gearbox
0 Name: gearbox.ldr
0 Author: erik-larsen
0 // A two-speed gearbox using the 3L driving ring system. The output shaft is a ridged 3L axle
0 // joiner (18948) with an axle in each end; a 24 tooth and a 16 tooth clutch gear spin freely
0 // on those axles, one each side of it. The driving ring (18947) slides on the joiner: shifted
0 // towards the 24 tooth gear it locks that gear to the shaft (first gear, 1:3, driven by the
0 // input's 8 tooth gear); towards the 16 tooth gear, second gear (1:1, driven by the input's
0 // 16 tooth gear); centred, neutral. The input axle is 2 studs (40 LDU) from the output shaft.
0 // A gear lever shifts it, as the 8880 Super Car's does: tilted into a slot of its gate, its
0 // foot swings the other way, into the ring, and slides it.

0 // Step 1: a 6x8 plate, with a 1x6 brick and a Technic 1x6 brick on top at each end
1 72 0 0 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3036.dat
1 14 0 -24 70 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3009.dat
1 14 0 -24 -70 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3009.dat
1 14 0 -48 70 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3894.dat
1 14 0 -48 -70 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3894.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 2: the output shaft: the joiner with the driving ring on it (centred: neutral), and
0 // a 4L axle in each end through the bricks
1 72 -20 -38 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 18948.dat
1 0 -20 -38 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 18947.dat
1 0 -20 -38 -50 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3705.dat
1 0 -20 -38 50 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3705.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 3: the clutch gears, free on the axles either side of the joiner
1 71 -20 -38 -40 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 2471.dat
1 71 -20 -38 40 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 18946.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 4: the input axle with an 8 tooth gear (meshing the 24 tooth clutch gear) and a 16
0 // tooth gear (meshing the 16 tooth clutch gear), each turned half a tooth to mesh
1 0 20 -38 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3707.dat
1 72 20 -38 -40 0.92388 -0.382683 0 0.382683 0.92388 0 0 0 1 3647.dat
1 71 20 -38 40 0.980785 -0.19509 0 0.19509 0.980785 0 0 0 1 4019.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 5: the stick shift. A 1x6 brick and a 1x6 plate on each end wall, and on each a 2x6 plate
0 // reaching in over the gears, carrying a gear shift gate plate (6543) above the driving ring.
0 // The 4 speed shift lever (6549) stands up through the gate, its ball in it, a cone on its
0 // stick for a knob, and its foot below the ball, beside the ring. Tilted into either slot on
0 // the input axle's side, its foot swings into the ring: towards the 24 tooth gear, first;
0 // towards the 16 tooth gear, second. The two slots on the other side swing it away from the
0 // ring, so they're neutral, like the middle.
1 14 0 -72 70 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3009.dat
1 14 0 -72 -70 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3009.dat
1 14 0 -80 70 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3666.dat
1 14 0 -80 -70 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3666.dat
1 14 0 -88 60 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3795.dat
1 14 0 -88 -60 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3795.dat
1 15 0 -96 0 0 0 -1 0 1 0 1 0 0 6543.dat
1 0 0 -73 0 -1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 -1 6549.dat
1 1 0 -164 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 4589.dat
0 STEP
